      "content": "I see what you're saying about \"sowing the seeds of moral rehabilitation,\" but it feels like you're still trying to steer the argument back to one side. You're essentially saying that even if the system is broken, you have to play along to fix it. Isn't there a real risk that by telling people they have a \"moral obligation\" to vote for \"tainted\" candidates, you're actually just legitimizing a broken status quo and discouraging the very change they want?",
